.TH LIBMPQ__BLOCK_VERIFY 3 2026-09-11 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__block_verify \- verify one sector and return its stored Adler-32
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__block_verify("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "block_number",
.BI "        uint32_t      *" "checksum",
.BI "        uint32_t      *" "mismatches"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly verify one sector against its stored MPQ sector checksum.
MPQ sector CRCs use Adler-32 over packed sector bytes after decryption and
before decompression. The optional checksum table may itself be compressed,
but is not encrypted. COMPRESS and PKWARE IMPLODE sectors are supported,
including encrypted sectors and MPQE archives.
.PP
The existing reader loads the table, reads and decrypts the selected sector,
compares its checksum, and decodes the sector. No other sector payload is
verified. This does not require (attributes) and does not check file CRC32
or MD5. Complete lossless file reads automatically check available CRC32/MD5
attributes; block reads do not perform file-level attribute verification.
.SH RETURN VALUE
LIBMPQ_SUCCESS means the operation completed. *checksum receives the stored
Adler-32, not the calculated value. *mismatches is zero for a match or
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_SECTOR_CRC for a mismatch. Checksums are not authentication.
.PP
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST means a NULL required argument, invalid file/block number,
or no usable sector checksum: absent table, missing sector-CRC flag,
single-unit or non-codec storage, or a zero/all-ones checksum entry.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED means a writer archive was supplied.
Malformed metadata, read, seek, decryption, decoding, size and allocation
failures retain the normal negative libmpq errors.
.PP
Both non-NULL output pointers are initialized to zero before validation.
Outputs are published only after the complete operation succeeds and remain
zero on any failure, even if a mismatch was detected before a decoding error.
Use separate storage for checksum and mismatches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__block_read (3),
.BR libmpq__file_blocks (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3)
